      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Express ${log}_{5}⁡2+{log}_{5}⁡4+{log}_{5}⁡6$ as a single logarithm.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡a+{log}_{n}⁡b={log}_{n}⁡(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule for logarithms, we can combine the first two terms as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡2+{log}_{5}⁡4+{log}_{5}⁡6 & ={log}_{5}⁡(2\\cdot 4)+{log}_{5}⁡6 \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡8+{log}_{5}⁡6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule for logarithms once more, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡8+{log}_{5}⁡6 & ={log}_{5}⁡(8\\cdot 6) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
